\section*{P. 89: the printed divisor $b$}
In the opening paragraph, the print says that $\psi$ is not divisible by $b$.
It does not print $\delta$ at this point. Both editions now reproduce $b$;
the S03 transcription's $\delta$ was an unmarked contextual repair.
The surrounding argument concerns a supposed common divisor $\delta$ of
$E$ and $F$, and the next sentence again names $\delta$. Thus $\delta$ appears
to be intended, but this is an editorial inference, not the diplomatic reading.

